; Release builds raise the inliner threshold (stock default is 10) so the tiny
; per-instruction helpers — U32.* (add/wrap/shl/...), has, set_flag, op_of_int —
; are inlined into the CPU hot loop. The stock, non-flambda compiler only inlines
; across modules under -inline, and these functions sit well under the cost
; threshold; 100 is enough (higher only bloats the varied boot path). ~+8% boot.

(env
 (release
  (ocamlopt_flags
   (:standard -inline 100))))
